{"parentUuid":"ac636aaa-3f82-4ce2-90ae-ac2898012a5c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_012xvPmp93u4XsCkJUF5poSs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A35XuX4w47QYoLJSXpv6L8","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"3D container loading extreme point heuristic caving degree benchmark BR Bischoff"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7457,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":171,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7457},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":171,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7457,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxnPs2YH6y8BAZ3BdJP","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9126ae74-640e-47a8-9b6e-525360f2784d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:00.523Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ac636aaa-3f82-4ce2-90ae-ac2898012a5c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H3sjh17H2MHisZk7YQBmSv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"3D bin packing problem ML deep reinforcement learning 2025 SOTA GOPT PCT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GOPT: Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing via Transformer-based Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.05344v2\"},{\"title\":\"GOPT: Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing via Transformer-Based Deep Reinforcement Learning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/384351006_GOPT_Generalizable_Online_3D_Bin_Packing_via_Transformer-Based_Deep_Reinforcement_Learning\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) GOPT: Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing via Transformer-based Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/383911136_GOPT_Generalizable_Online_3D_Bin_Packing_via_Transformer-based_Deep_Reinforcement_Learning\"},{\"title\":\"Heuristics Integrated Deep Reinforcement Learning for Online 3D Bin Packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/367199162_Heuristics_Integrated_Deep_Reinforcement_Learning_for_Online_3D_Bin_Packing\"},{\"title\":\"Adjustable Robust Reinforcement Learning for Online 3D Bin Packing Yuxin Pan1\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2023/file/a345ed605675c7c484e740a8ceaa6b45-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] GOPT: Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing via Transformer-Based Deep Reinforcement Learning | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/GOPT:-Generalizable-Online-3D-Bin-Packing-via-Deep-Xiong-Guo/df8cebc7bea702680fa1d0ee7e21e64b67792ac1\"},{\"title\":\"A deep reinforcement learning approach for online and concurrent 3D bin packing optimisation with bin replacement strategies - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0166361524001301\"},{\"title\":\"One4Many-StablePacker: An Efficient Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework for the 3D Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.10057v1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Xiong5Heng/GOPT: [IEEE RA-L 2024] GOPT: Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing via Transformer-based Deep Reinforcement Learning · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Xiong5Heng/GOPT\"},{\"title\":\"Online 3D Bin Packing with Constrained Deep Reinforcement Learning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/363394218_Online_3D_Bin_Packing_with_Constrained_Deep_Reinforcement_Learning\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding the 3D bin packing problem with machine learning and deep reinforcement learning:\n\n## Key Methods and SOTA\n\n**GOPT (Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing)** is a prominent state-of-the-art approach. GOPT is a generalizable online 3D Bin Packing approach via Transformer-based deep reinforcement learning (DRL) that proposes a Packing Transformer, which fuses the features of the items and bin, to identify the spatial correlation between the item to be packed and available sub-spaces within the bin.\n\n**PCT (Packing Configuration Tree)** is another key baseline method. The Packing Configuration Tree (PCT) is based on heuristic search rules and is incorporated into a DRL agent.\n\n## 2025 Developments\n\nRecent work includes the One4Many-StablePacker (O4M-SP) framework, where \"One4Many\" denotes the model's ability to generalize across bins with varied dimensions, and \"Stable\" emphasizes the model's explicit integration of stability-related constraints to ensure real-world feasibility.\n\n## Key Technical Components\n\nGOPT employs the Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) algorithm to train the approach. GOPT first proposes free sub-spaces within a bin and utilizes a modified Transformer to discern the relations among these spaces and the relations between them and the current item.\n\nThe research indicates that these DRL-based methods have progressed significantly in handling generalization across different bin dimensions and incorporating real-world constraints like stability.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"627b6186-56f7-4b46-8f86-d0e1f5f0d428","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:06.778Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ac636aaa-3f82-4ce2-90ae-ac2898012a5c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9126ae74-640e-47a8-9b6e-525360f2784d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A35XuX4w47QYoLJSXpv6L8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"3D container loading extreme point heuristic caving degree benchmark BR Bischoff\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A caving degree approach for the single container loading problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221708002282\"},{\"title\":\"A caving degree approach for the single container loading problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/222045985_A_caving_degree_approach_for_the_single_container_loading_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Extreme Point-Based Heuristics for Three-Dimensional Bin Packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220668799_Extreme_Point-Based_Heuristics_for_Three-Dimensional_Bin_Packing\"},{\"title\":\"Extreme Point-Based Heuristics for Three-Dimensional Bin ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cirrelt.ca/documentstravail/cirrelt-2007-41.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A comparative review of 3D container loading algorithms - Zhao - 2016 - International Transactions in Operational Research - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/itor.12094\"},{\"title\":\"The Three-Dimensional Container Loading Problem Xiaozhou Zhao\",\"url\":\"https://eprints.soton.ac.uk/413542/1/Final_PhD_thesis.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Extreme Point-Based Heuristics for Three-Dimensional Bin Packing | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.1070.0250\"},{\"title\":\"Extreme Point-based Heuristics for Three-Dimensional Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/11385818.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Solving the single-container loading problem by a fast heuristic method\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/232988135_Solving_the_single-container_loading_problem_by_a_fast_heuristic_method\"},{\"title\":\"An efficient placement heuristic for three-dimensional rectangular packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/262400354_An_efficient_placement_heuristic_for_three-dimensional_rectangular_packing\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant research on these topics related to 3D container loading:\n\n## Caving Degree Approach\n\nA new heuristic approach has been proposed for solving the three-dimensional single container loading problem, with the key issue being to pack items into a corner or even a cave in the container such that items are packed as compactly and closely as possible with other packed items. The caving degree represents the cavity degree of an action that packs an item into a layer of the container, such that the item is packed as compactly as possible to other items already packed.\n\n## Benchmark Results (BR Bischoff)\n\nFor the 47 without-orientation-constraint instances from the OR-Library, experiments indicate an average packing utilization of 94.9%, which improves current best result reported in the literature by 3.9%. For the 800 strongly heterogeneous instances among 1500 representative benchmarks proposed by Bischoff et al., experiments show an average packing utilization of 87.97%, which improves current best record reported in the literature by 0.28%.\n\n## Extreme Point Heuristic\n\nThe extreme point concept provides a new extreme point-based rule for packing items inside a three-dimensional container that is independent from the particular packing problem addressed and can handle additional constraints, and is used to derive new constructive heuristics for the three-dimensional bin-packing problem. The Extreme Points idea extends the Corner Points concept and provides the means to exploit the free space defined inside a packing by the shapes of the items already in the container.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a4accf6b-b8bd-42c1-9535-4b784958eaff","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:08.221Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9126ae74-640e-47a8-9b6e-525360f2784d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
