{"parentUuid":"6dea5be2-1538-4e06-9400-eaed79e84a7e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Quuryi5ym6UobwpzaUX9RK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0188Vfr3wHL2Qb1354o1iAji","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"conditional query learning\" 3D bin packing reinforcement learning attention"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3232,"cache_read_input_tokens":20578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3232,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":48,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxoQH7B9B2wT5MrNtCy","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"196248ad-e605-4ce6-834b-71e0d27b4ef6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:14.132Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"196248ad-e605-4ce6-834b-71e0d27b4ef6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0188Vfr3wHL2Qb1354o1iAji","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"conditional query learning\" 3D bin packing reinforcement learning attention\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solving Packing Problems by Conditional Query Learning | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=BkgTwRNtPB\"},{\"title\":\"ONE MODEL PACKS THOUSANDS OF ITEMS WITH RECURRENT CONDITIONAL QUERY LEARNING\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2111.06726\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Offline 3D Bin Packing Problem with Large-sized Bin via Two-stage Deep Reinforcement Learning | Proceedings of the 23rd International Conference on Autonomous Agents and Multiagent Systems\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.5555/3635637.3663232\"},{\"title\":\"One4Many-StablePacker: An Efficient Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework for the 3D Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.10057v1\"},{\"title\":\"Three-dimensional bin packing problem with variable bin height | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/229324130_Three-dimensional_bin_packing_problem_with_variable_bin_height\"},{\"title\":\"Deep Reinforcement Learning Method with Integrated Rotation and Placement Strategies for Solving the 2D Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397874286_Deep_Reinforcement_Learning_Method_with_Integrated_Rotation_and_Placement_Strategies_for_Solving_the_2D_Bin_Packing_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"One model packs thousands of items with Recurrent Conditional Query Learning - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S095070512100945X\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning for the Multi-Dimensional Bin Packing Problem: Literature Review and Empirical Evaluation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.08103v1\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) One model Packs Thousands of Items with Recurrent Conditional Query Learning\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/356198097_One_model_Packs_Thousands_of_Items_with_Recurrent_Conditional_Query_Learning\"},{\"title\":\"A Dynamic Multi-modal deep Reinforcement Learning framework for 3D Bin Packing Problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0950705124006245\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about conditional query learning for 3D bin packing with reinforcement learning and attention:\n\n## Overview\n\nConditional Query Learning (CQL) is a method designed to handle the packing problem for both 2D and 3D settings. By embedding previous actions as a conditional query to the attention model, researchers designed a fully end-to-end model and trained it for 2D and 3D packing via reinforcement learning.\n\n## Key Technical Approach\n\nThe Recurrent Conditional Query Learning (RCQL) method solves both 2D and 3D packing problems by first embedding states with a recurrent encoder, and then adopting attention with conditional queries from previous actions. The conditional query mechanism fills the information gap between learning steps, which shapes the problem as a Markov decision process.\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nConditional query learning addresses a key challenge: traditional neural combinatorial optimization is less efficient for more complicated problems such as packing, one type of optimization problem that faces mutual conditioned action space.\n\n## Performance Results\n\nThe method achieves lower bin gap ratio and variance for both 2D and 3D packing, improving 7.2% space utilization ratio compared with genetic algorithm for 3D packing (30 boxes case), and reduces more than 10% bin gap ratio in almost every case compared with extant learning approaches.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a32be83e-1e79-4d2f-8af5-6507e2d38010","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:21.252Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"196248ad-e605-4ce6-834b-71e0d27b4ef6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6dea5be2-1538-4e06-9400-eaed79e84a7e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FFdV1VPE2gAkmn7cDmcAZ1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"3D bin packing logic-based Benders decomposition LBBD Lufthansa ULD scheduling 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_17\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders decomposition for single machine scheduling in additive manufacturing with two-dimensional packing constraints - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221724003394\"},{\"title\":\"OPUS 4 | ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\",\"url\":\"https://opus4.kobv.de/opus4-zib/frontdoor/index/index/docId/9643\"},{\"title\":\"Accelerated Benders Decomposition for Variable-Height ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2308.01104\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders decomposition for single machine scheduling in additive manufacturing with two-dimensional packing constraints\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v317y2024i3p890-905.html\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders Decomposition for the Two-Dimensional Bin Packing Problem | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2020.1014\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dwave-examples/3d-bin-packing: Use the minimum number of bins to pack items with different dimensions, weights and properties. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dwave-examples/3d-bin-packing\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders' decomposition for the constrained two-dimensional non-guillotine cutting problem with defects\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/taf/tprsxx/v62y2024i23p8299-8325.html\"},{\"title\":\"Solving the parallel processor scheduling and bin packing problems\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Solving-the-PPSP-and-the-BPP-with-contiguity-constraints-2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"}]\n\nI found highly relevant research on your topic. Here are the key results:\n\n## Main Result: ULD Build-Up Scheduling with Logic-Based Benders Decomposition\n\nA logic-based Benders decomposition approach has been proposed that assigns batches to time intervals and workstations in the master problem, while the actual schedule is decided in a subproblem, presented at the Integration of Constraint Programming, Artificial Intelligence, and Operations Research (CPAIOR 2024) conference.\n\n### Problem Context\n\nThe research addresses a complex planning and scheduling problem arising from the build-up process of air cargo pallets and containers (ULDs), where ULD build-ups must be scheduled neither too early to avoid underutilizing ULD capacity, nor too late to avoid resource conflicts with other flights.\n\n### Solution Approach\n\nThe logic-based Benders decomposition approach assigns batches to time intervals and workstations in the master problem, while the actual schedule is decided in a subproblem. By choosing appropriate intervals, the subproblem becomes a feasibility problem that decomposes over the workstations, and the similarity of many batches is exploited by a strengthening procedure for no-good cuts.\n\n### Performance Results\n\nThe approach was benchmarked against a time-expanded MIP formulation from the literature on a publicly available data set, solving 15% more instances to optimality and decreasing run times by more than 50% in the geometric mean.\n\n## Authors\n\nThe research was conducted by Euler, R., Borndörfer, R., and Puchert, C. (2024).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f2216031-e12d-40c4-ba32-f41a983cc4b2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:21.404Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6dea5be2-1538-4e06-9400-eaed79e84a7e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
