{"parentUuid":"3d8e7bff-cfba-46fc-b34e-bb256d061b0c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GnZkcSCBoA73NRaUaqGWmH","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"3D bin packing constraint programming CP-SAT large neighborhood search 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Guided Local Search for the Three-Dimensional Bin-Packing Problem | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.15.3.267.16080\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive large neighborhood search for solving the circle bin packing problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/347835809_Adaptive_large_neighborhood_search_for_solving_the_circle_bin_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Consistent neighborhood search for one-dimensional bin packing and two-dimensional vector packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/305847208_Consistent_neighborhood_search_for_one-dimensional_bin_packing_and_two-dimensional_vector_packing\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) TSpack: A Unified Tabu Search Code for Multi-Dimensional Bin Packing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/44707057_TSpack_A_Unified_Tabu_Search_Code_for_Multi-Dimensional_Bin_Packing_Problems\"},{\"title\":\"Exact Solution of the Two-Dimensional Finite Bin Packing Problem | Management Science\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/abs/10.1287/mnsc.44.3.388\"},{\"title\":\"The Three-Dimensional Bin Packing Problem | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.48.2.256.12386\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A New Heuristic Algorithm for the 3D Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/226249396_A_New_Heuristic_Algorithm_for_the_3D_Bin_Packing_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"Solving the parallel processor scheduling and bin packing problems with contiguity constraints: Mathematical models and computational studies - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724007161\"},{\"title\":\"One4Many-StablePacker: An Efficient Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework for the 3D Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.10057v1\"},{\"title\":\"Spatial Genius: How 3D Packing Transforms Shipping\",\"url\":\"http://www.ijlret.com/Papers/Vol-11-issue-08/11.D2025586.pdf\"}]\n\nI've performed a web search on 3D bin packing with constraint programming and large neighborhood search techniques for 2024-2025. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent Research in 3D Bin Packing\n\nThe search results show several important developments in this field:\n\n### Constraint Programming and CP-SAT Approaches\n\nWhile the results don't specifically highlight CP-SAT (Google's Constraint Programming Solver), they do show that constraint programming models have been developed for the container loading problem, with a block-building constraint programming model for the container loading problem published in 2025.\n\n### Large Neighborhood Search Methods\n\nTailored adaptive large neighborhood search (TALNS) algorithms combining adaptive large neighborhood search and tabu search have been proposed for related packing problems, with TALNS generating high-quality solutions in much shorter time than CPLEX.\n\n### Recent Developments (2024-2025)\n\nThe research landscape includes:\n- Machine learning approaches for multi-dimensional bin packing problems\n- Comparative analysis of heuristics and metaheuristics including GA and HALNS, alongside DRL models for online formulations\n- Recent work on deliberate planning of 3D bin packing on packing configuration trees\n\nThe results suggest active research combining classical optimization techniques with modern machine learning approaches, though specific recent publications explicitly focused on CP-SAT with large neighborhood search were not directly highlighted in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b9d5ebde-77ee-414b-987e-18e75a9168f1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:31.055Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3d8e7bff-cfba-46fc-b34e-bb256d061b0c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2beb6f37-d99d-48d7-b997-2ca62b0fe6c1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqLXjcdp5AuTDwWjRgKHiK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Amazon DHL FedEx 3D bin packing industrial production deployment 2024 algorithm\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"3D Printing - DHL - United States of America\",\"url\":\"https://www.dhl.com/us-en/home/innovation-in-logistics/logistics-trend-radar/3d-printing-logistics.html\"},{\"title\":\"3D packaging simulation success stories with DHL - Visual Components\",\"url\":\"https://www.visualcomponents.com/case-studies/dhl-3d-packaging-simulation-success-stories/\"},{\"title\":\"Top 10: Automated Warehouses | Supply Chain Magazine\",\"url\":\"https://supplychaindigital.com/top10/top-10-automated-warehouses-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon takes aim at the supply chain\",\"url\":\"https://www.axios.com/2026/05/05/amazon-logistics-ups-fedex\"},{\"title\":\"Dhl\",\"url\":\"https://www.dhl.com/content/dam/dhl/global/core/documents/pdf/glo-core-rethinking-packaging-trend-report.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"TREND RADAR 5th Edition LOGISTICS THE Delivering insight today,\",\"url\":\"https://www.dhl.com/content/dam/dhl/global/core/documents/pdf/glo-core-logistics-trend-radar-5thedition.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Dynamic 3D Load Optimization Using AI and Heuristic Integration in Smart Logistics | Journal of Human, Earth, and Future\",\"url\":\"https://www.hefjournal.org/index.php/HEF/article/view/556\"},{\"title\":\"Logistics Trends 2023/2024: Which Direction for AI? | DHL Freight\",\"url\":\"https://dhl-freight-connections.com/en/trends/logistics-trends-2023-2024/\"},{\"title\":\"The Future of Smart Warehousing: How FedEx and DHL Are Revolutionizing B2B Logistics\",\"url\":\"https://www.cleverence.com/articles/business-blogs/the-future-of-smart-warehousing-how-fedex-and-dhl-are-revolutionizing-b2b-logistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Next-generation Packaging - DHL - United Kingdom\",\"url\":\"https://www.dhl.com/gb-en/home/innovation-in-logistics/logistics-trend-radar/next-generation-advanced-packaging.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found information related to your query about 3D bin packing and logistics automation, though the results don't specifically focus on 3D bin packing algorithm deployment by Amazon, DHL, and FedEx together.\n\nHere's what I found:\n\n## 3D Bin Packing in Logistics\n\nEfficient 3D bin packing remains a significant challenge in logistics, supply chain management, and warehouse automation, where the objective is to maximize space utilization and maintain load stability while minimizing computational time. Recent research has explored advanced algorithmic approaches to address this challenge.\n\nA Hybrid PPO algorithm demonstrates balanced performance, achieving high placement success rates and superior stability scores, outperforming traditional methods and standalone genetic algorithms by combining intelligent learning with domain-specific heuristics. This hybrid approach positions itself as a promising and scalable solution for real-world logistics environments demanding both efficiency and adaptability in 3D load optimization.\n\n## Industrial Deployment by Major Logistics Companies\n\nWhile specific 3D bin packing algorithm deployments weren't detailed in 2024:\n\n- DHL uses robotic arms and automated systems for various warehouse tasks, with AI-powered systems that use data to continuously optimize processes.\n\n- FedEx employs automated sorting systems and robotic systems, along with AI-powered systems that can predict demand and optimize inventory levels in real time.\n\n- DHL's Robotics Hub orchestrates robotics and digital automation technologies across its warehouse operations, including assisted picking robots and wrapping robots.\n\nThe search results indicate active development in AI-driven logistics optimization but don't reveal specific 2024 industrial deployments of 3D bin packing algorithms across these companies.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"971a5a9d-39ac-4f26-931f-a3939aff18f4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:32.789Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2beb6f37-d99d-48d7-b997-2ca62b0fe6c1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
