{"parentUuid":"79b1a022-e8e5-49de-a3bb-ea7aacae8524","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RzhUKN78953kVrsfuYpYDq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A9VZbiZVoscj7vg5jPHR4m","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"3D container loading wall-building floor-building layer heuristic guillotine block"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4518,"cache_read_input_tokens":25420,"output_tokens":164,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4518},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":164,"cache_read_input_tokens":25420,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4518,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxqDARrYh3MeMFNmexx","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a80b29ad-5d85-492d-867d-6758c6ed688d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:37.437Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"79b1a022-e8e5-49de-a3bb-ea7aacae8524","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019q8k6o9B9ByTLjntG8hECs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"packing configuration tree\" PCT online 3D bin packing deliberate planning hierarchical\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - alexfrom0815/Online-3D-BPP-PCT: Code implementation of \\\"Learning Efficient Online 3D Bin Packing on Packing Configuration Trees\\\". We propose to enhance the practical applicability of online 3D Bin Packing Problem (BPP) via learning on a hierarchical packing configuration tree which makes the deep reinforcement learning (DRL) model easy to deal with practical constraints and well-performing even with continuous solution space.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/alexfrom0815/Online-3D-BPP-PCT\"},{\"title\":\"[2504.04421] Deliberate Planning of 3D Bin Packing on Packing Configuration Trees\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.04421\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Efficient Online 3D Bin Packing on Packing Configuration Trees | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=bfuGjlCwAq\"},{\"title\":\"Deliberate Planning of 3D Bin Packing on Packing Configuration Trees\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.04421\"},{\"title\":\"Deliberate planning of 3D bin packing on packing configuration trees - Hang Zhao, Juzhan Xu, Kexiong Yu, Ruizhen Hu, Chenyang Zhu, Bo Du, Kai Xu, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/02783649251380619\"},{\"title\":\"[2504.04421v1] Deliberate Planning of 3D Bin Packing on Packing Configuration Trees\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.04421v1\"},{\"title\":\"[Literature Review] Deliberate Planning of 3D Bin Packing on Packing Configuration Trees\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/en/review/deliberate-planning-of-3d-bin-packing-on-packing-configuration-trees\"},{\"title\":\"LEARNING EFFICIENT ONLINE 3D BIN PACKING\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=bfuGjlCwAq\"},{\"title\":\"Deliberate Planning of 3D Bin Packing on Packing Configuration Trees | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/390570126_Deliberate_Planning_of_3D_Bin_Packing_on_Packing_Configuration_Trees\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Deliberate Planning of 3D Bin Packing on Packing Configuration Trees | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Deliberate-Planning-of-3D-Bin-Packing-on-Packing-Zhao-Xu/f848210eba3fcc0e7321667d53a2f3fe8b5333e6\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's comprehensive information about Packing Configuration Tree (PCT) and online 3D bin packing:\n\n## Overview\n\nPCT is a novel hierarchical representation designed to enhance the practical applicability of online 3D bin packing. PCT is a dynamically growing tree where the internal nodes describe the space configurations of packed items and leaf nodes the packable placements of the current item.\n\n## Key Technical Features\n\nPCT is a full-fledged description of the state and action space of bin packing which can support packing policy learning based on deep reinforcement learning (DRL). The size of the packing action space is proportional to the number of leaf nodes, making the DRL model easy to train and well-performing even with continuous solution space.\n\n## Learning Approach\n\nThe approach enhances the practical applicability of online 3D bin packing problem (BPP) via learning on a hierarchical packing configuration tree which makes the deep reinforcement learning (DRL) model easy to deal with practical constraints and well-performing even with continuous solution space.\n\n## Deliberate Planning\n\nPCT can function as tree-based planners in deliberately solving packing problems of industrial significance, including large-scale packing and different variations of BPP setting. A recursive packing method is proposed to decompose large-scale packing into regular sub-trees while a spatial ensemble mechanism integrates local solutions into a global one. For different BPP variations with additional decision variables, such as lookahead, buffering, and offline packing, a unified planning framework enables various problem-solving based on a pre-trained PCT model with no additional adaptation.\n\n## Real-World Applications\n\nA real-world packing robot for industrial warehousing was developed, with careful designs accounting for constrained placement and transportation stability. The packing robot operates reliably and efficiently on unprotected pallets at 10 seconds per box, achieving averagely 19 boxes per pallet with 57.4% space utilization for relatively large-size boxes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0735f00a-3b96-47d8-bc1a-e1a9cc83dd08","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:44.322Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"79b1a022-e8e5-49de-a3bb-ea7aacae8524","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a80b29ad-5d85-492d-867d-6758c6ed688d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A9VZbiZVoscj7vg5jPHR4m","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"3D container loading wall-building floor-building layer heuristic guillotine block\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A heuristic block-loading algorithm based on multi-layer search for the container loading problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220472098_A_heuristic_block-loading_algorithm_based_on_multi-layer_search_for_the_container_loading_problem\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A modified wall-building-based compound approach for the knapsack container loading problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/287996192_A_modified_wall-building-based_compound_approach_for_the_knapsack_container_loading_problem\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Modified Wall Building-Based Compound Approach for Container Loading Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/268685795_A_Modified_Wall_Building-Based_Compound_Approach_for_Container_Loading_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Modified Wall Building-Based Compound Approach for Container Loading Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/68379820/A_Modified_Wall_Building_Based_Compound_Approach_for_Container_Loading_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"A heuristic block-loading algorithm based on multi-layer search for the container loading problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054811003078\"},{\"title\":\"The six elements to block-building approaches for the single container loading problem | Applied Intelligence | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10489-012-0337-0\"},{\"title\":\"A randomized heuristic for the container loading problem: Further investigations\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/237300694_A_randomized_heuristic_for_the_container_loading_problem_Further_investigations\"},{\"title\":\"A Tree Search Algorithm for Solving the Container Loading Problem | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.1090.0338\"},{\"title\":\"A two-dimensional heuristic decomposition approach to a three-dimensional multiple container loading problem | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/305628446_A_two-dimensional_heuristic_decomposition_approach_to_a_three-dimensional_multiple_container_loading_problem\"},{\"title\":\"A block-based layer building approach for the 2D guillotine strip packing problem | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/A-block-based-layer-building-approach-for-the-2D-Wei-Tian/2e3db961c296a5bd4b12d15edf46bca7ee282df8\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I've found substantial academic research on 3D container loading optimization. Here's what the literature reveals about these key heuristic approaches:\n\n## Main Heuristic Approaches\n\nThe major methodologies include horizontal layer building approaches that fill containers with layers from bottom to top, stack building approaches that arrange boxes into stacks on the container floor, and the guillotine cutting approach based on a slicing tree representation where branches correspond to guillotine partitioning of container regions.\n\n## Wall-Building and Floor-Building Methods\n\nModified wall-building based approaches perform multiple wall-building heuristics with different ranking functions and priority rules, with six orthogonal rotations of containers equivalent to filling the container in four wall building methods and two floor building methods.\n\n## Block-Building Approaches\n\nThe block-building approach constructs blocks composed of one or two types of boxes that are tightly packed, which are then placed in the container. In the Single Container Loading Problem, many recently successful techniques share a similar structure involving the use of blocks of boxes.\n\n## Multi-Layer Search\n\nEfficient heuristic block-loading algorithms based on multi-layer search load one block determined by a block selecting algorithm in each packing phase, with the concept of composite blocks that can contain multiple types of boxes under restrictions, and a multi-layer search algorithm developed based on depth-first search.\n\nThese approaches address the optimization of 3D container loading while satisfying constraints like full support, guillotine cutting, and orientation restrictions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"408a49fc-c9ab-4b8c-9809-91c6d4c1c7b3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:44.856Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a80b29ad-5d85-492d-867d-6758c6ed688d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"408a49fc-c9ab-4b8c-9809-91c6d4c1c7b3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01X8aR9DEQrgUt1UpchKhpXP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough to compile the analysis. Let me do one final targeted search on the gravity/support analog."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3407,"cache_read_input_tokens":29938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3407,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoxr6KwRHs1FA36q1jh1","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b591d881-734b-4767-b8d8-107a43cb3b10","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:48.023Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b591d881-734b-4767-b8d8-107a43cb3b10","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01X8aR9DEQrgUt1UpchKhpXP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CVJZ7xqLuwZJuZj8irhTcD","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"3D bin packing stability support constraint full base contact 2024 hybrid heuristic ML"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3407,"cache_read_input_tokens":29938,"output_tokens":127,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3407},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":127,"cache_read_input_tokens":29938,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3407,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoxr6KwRHs1FA36q1jh1","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"efed681e-9721-4f70-82ea-bde3d1538b9a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:48.808Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"efed681e-9721-4f70-82ea-bde3d1538b9a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"88dcafdf-a08f-4678-84c0-930bce6a1767","agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CVJZ7xqLuwZJuZj8irhTcD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"3D bin packing stability support constraint full base contact 2024 hybrid heuristic ML\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Integrating Heuristic Methods with Deep Reinforcement Learning for Online 3D Bin-Packing Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/1424-8220/24/16/5370\"},{\"title\":\"One4Many-StablePacker: An Efficient Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework for the 3D Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.10057v1\"},{\"title\":\"Integrating Heuristic Methods with Deep Reinforcement Learning for Online 3D Bin-Packing Optimization - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11358981/\"},{\"title\":\"Solving a 3D bin packing problem with stacking constraints - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360835223008380\"},{\"title\":\"Static stability versus packing efficiency in online three-dimensional packing problems: A new approach and a computational study - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054825000334\"},{\"title\":\"Dynamic 3D Load Optimization Using AI and Heuristic Integration in Smart Logistics | Journal of Human, Earth, and Future\",\"url\":\"https://www.hefjournal.org/index.php/HEF/article/view/556\"},{\"title\":\"Online 3D Bin Packing with Fast Stability Validation and Stable Rearrangement Planning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.09123v1\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Learning for the Multi-Dimensional Bin Packing Problem: Literature Review and Empirical Evaluation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2312.08103v1\"},{\"title\":\"Extreme Point-Based Heuristics for Three-Dimensional Bin Packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220668799_Extreme_Point-Based_Heuristics_for_Three-Dimensional_Bin_Packing\"},{\"title\":\"Solving a 3D bin packing problem with stacking constraints | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/376214606_Solving_a_3D_bin_packing_problem_with_stacking_constraints\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive research on 3D bin packing with stability constraints and hybrid machine learning approaches. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent 2024 Research\n\nA prominent study proposes a method named Hybrid Heuristic Proximal Policy Optimization (HHPPO) to implement online 3D bin-packing tasks, integrating heuristic algorithms for bin-packing with the Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) algorithm of deep reinforcement learning.\n\n## Stability Constraints Approaches\n\nThe research distinguishes between different support constraint models:\n\n1. **Full Base Contact vs. Partial Support**: Traditional methods use complete support constraints requiring the bottom of the object be fully supported by other objects or the container itself, prohibiting overhanging placements; however, complete support constraints overly restrict space utilization and limit flexibility, so partial support constraints are introduced to allow more effective space use while maintaining stability.\n\n2. **Advanced Constraint Types**: Research focuses on developing heuristic methods under distinct static stability constraints, including full-base support, partial-base support, and center-of-gravity polygon support.\n\n## Hybrid ML Integration\n\nThe HHPPO method proposes an extreme point priority sorting method to improve space utilization, and uses a 3D grid representation of container space status with partial support constraints to increase stacking possibilities.\n\nThe Hybrid PPO algorithm demonstrates balanced performance with 100% placement success in the smallest container and over 72.4% in the largest, while the Hybrid PPO model outperforms traditional methods by combining intelligent learning with domain-specific heuristics.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0650854e-d328-4e8b-a50a-9d704f8fbf57","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:56.459Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"efed681e-9721-4f70-82ea-bde3d1538b9a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0650854e-d328-4e8b-a50a-9d704f8fbf57","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a05e4fa8a42244885","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014LRhBXaij21ZP3ZimHGWYE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sufficient material gathered. Compiling the analysis.\n\n---\n\n# 3D Bin Packing 文献向 2D placement 的迁移评估\n\n**问题对偶性提醒：** 3D BPP 的核心约束是「重力/支撑/堆叠稳定性」，垂直方向是「次序+物理」；我们 70x70 是平面问题，但有「端口对齐 + 流量路由 + 强制设施 266 实例」——3D 中的「堆叠次序」对偶到我们的「先放骨架再嵌入填充」。\n\n## 7 个方法迁移评估\n\n### 1. Extreme Point Heuristic (Crainic, Perboli, Tadei 2008, INFORMS JoC) — 学术评分 9/10，迁移性 8/10\nextreme point 扩展 corner point，每放一块就在该块投影出的所有「凹角」生成新候选点。**迁移点：** 我们 outer_search 现在用 candidate_placements.json 静态枚举；改成「动态 extreme point」可以让强制设施放完后，自动收缩 ghost rectangle 候选集，省掉 exploratory 缓存。**关键论文：** [Extreme Point-Based Heuristics for 3D BP (CIRRELT 2007-41)](https://www.cirrelt.ca/documentstravail/cirrelt-2007-41.pdf)\n\n### 2. Caving Degree (He & Huang 2010, EJOR) — 学术评分 7/10，迁移性 9/10 ⭐\n评估每个候选点的「凹陷度」：物件嵌入「洞」越深得分越高。BR benchmark 平均利用率 87.97%（强非齐次实例）。**对 2D 的对偶：** 我们 ghost rectangle 需要找空 6x6+ 矩形——caving degree 反过来用，可以引导 mandatory 设施往「填洞」方向走，把零散空间挤到一起形成大矩形。**这条对 binding/routing 强约束几乎零冲突**。[A caving degree approach (EJOR 2008)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221708002282)\n\n### 3. PCT — Packing Configuration Tree (Zhao et al., ICLR 2022 + IJRR 2025) — 学术评分 9/10，迁移性 4/10\n层级树状态/动作空间，DRL 在叶子节点采样。2025 年 \"Deliberate Planning\" 版本支持 lookahead/buffer/offline。**问题：** 是 online 顺序放置范式，跟我们 Benders 全局最优范式相冲突；而且我们已经禁止 AI 写检查点（CLAUDE.md 安全合约）。最多作为 candidate ordering 的 hints 来源。[arXiv 2504.04421](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.04421)\n\n### 4. GOPT (Xiong et al., RA-L 2024) — 学术评分 8/10，迁移性 3/10\nTransformer + PPO，处理 sub-space 关系。**问题：** 跟 PCT 同病——online/RL 范式，对我们 max_lex(area, min_side) 的精确目标不适用。能用的只是 attention 思想：候选点之间的几何相关性可以做特征。[arXiv 2409.05344](https://arxiv.org/html/2409.05344v2)\n\n### 5. Recurrent Conditional Query Learning (Li et al., KBS 2022) — 学术评分 7/10，迁移性 5/10\nattention 模型把「上一步动作」作为 conditional query 嵌入。**有用的点：** 我们 S4 AI dataset v0 在做特征提取，可以借这个 query 设计——把「已放置的 mandatory 子集」作为 query 去预测下一个候选的边际收益。但仍是 shadow-only，不能改证明源。[arXiv 2111.06726](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2111.06726)\n\n### 6. ULD Build-Up Scheduling LBBD (Euler, Borndörfer, Puchert, CPAIOR 2024) — 学术评分 8/10，迁移性 9/10 ⭐\nMaster 分配批次到时间窗+工位，Subproblem 是可行性分解+ no-good cut 强化。比时间扩展 MIP 多解 15% 实例、运行时间缩 50%+。**对我们的迁移：** 这个 no-good cut 强化（\"similarity of many batches\" 利用对称性）正对应我们 binding_subproblem 的端口对称——同型号设施 binding 失败的 cut 应该能广播到所有同构候选，目前我们 benders_loop 是否做了 cut 强化值得审视。[Springer CPAIOR 2024](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_17)\n\n### 7. Block-Building / Composite Blocks (Wei, Zhang et al., COR 2014; Bortfeldt 多篇) — 学术评分 7/10，迁移性 6/10\n预先把 1-2 种 box 组成紧密 block，再把 block 当原子单元放置。**对偶到我们：** 把同型号 mandatory 设施聚合成「设施簇 block」，先放 block 再放散件——可能减少 master 的对称破坏负担。但要小心：这会改变 candidate_placements 的语义边界，必须走 PROJECT_LOCK 流程。[Six elements to block-building (Applied Intelligence 2013)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10489-012-0337-0)\n\n### 8. Combinatorial Benders for 2D BPP (Côté, Haouari, Iori, IJoC 2021) — 学术评分 9/10，迁移性 10/10 ⭐⭐\n**这个其实是 2D 的，但用了 3D 文献的 Benders 思想反流。** 把 packing 拆成「物件→bin 分配」master 和「bin 内可行性」sub。**对我们：** 这正是 benders_loop.py 的近亲——值得直接对照他们的 cut 生成方式（特别是 \"infeasibility certificate via reduced patterns\"），看我们 binding→routing→flow 链能否引入更紧的 combinatorial cut。[INFORMS IJoC](https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2020.1014)\n\n---\n\n## 末尾：对 2D placement 真正有用的是哪 1-2 条\n\n**真正高 ROI 的是这两条，按优先级：**\n\n1. **Caving Degree 引导 ghost rectangle 形成（迁移性 9/10）** — 直接对偶有用、零安全风险、不碰证明源，可以作为 outer_search 的 candidate ordering 信号（符合 AI 安全合约里的 order_only）。落地工作量 1-2 周。**这是首选。**\n\n2. **CPAIOR 2024 ULD LBBD 的 no-good cut 强化（迁移性 9/10）** — 直接强化 benders_loop.py 的求解效率，对 max_lex(area, min_side) 精确目标完全兼容（不像 RL 那一票）。需要审视当前 cut 是否利用了端口/设施对称性。落地需要碰 binding_subproblem，工作量 2-3 周但收益大。\n\n**明确不建议迁移的：** PCT/GOPT/RCQL 这一票 DRL 路线对我们 Phase 3B 精确证明目标基本无用，最多是 S4 AI sidecar 里做 shadow 实验——但那已经在做了，没必要把 3D 文献的复杂度引进来。\n\n---\n\nSources:\n- [Extreme Point-Based Heuristics for 3D BP (CIRRELT)](https://www.cirrelt.ca/documentstravail/cirrelt-2007-41.pdf)\n- [A caving degree approach (EJOR)](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221708002282)\n- [PCT — Deliberate Planning of 3D BPP (arXiv 2504.04421)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.04421)\n- [GOPT — Transformer DRL for 3D BPP (arXiv 2409.05344)](https://arxiv.org/html/2409.05344v2)\n- [Recurrent Conditional Query Learning (arXiv 2111.06726)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2111.06726)\n- [ULD Build-Up Scheduling LBBD (CPAIOR 2024)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_17)\n- [Six elements to block-building (Applied Intelligence)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10489-012-0337-0)\n- [Combinatorial Benders for 2D BPP (INFORMS IJoC)](https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.2020.1014)\n- [HHPPO Hybrid Heuristic + DRL (Sensors 2024)](https://www.mdpi.com/1424-8220/24/16/5370)\n- [One4Many-StablePacker (arXiv 2510.10057)](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.10057v1)\n- [ML for Multi-Dimensional BPP literature review (arXiv 2312.08103)](https://arxiv.org/html/2312.08103v1)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1552,"cache_read_input_tokens":33345,"output_tokens":3224,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1552},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3224,"cache_read_input_tokens":33345,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1552,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxrxJGpn6c5r2nayMDo","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"41742ba3-d235-4b4c-9f05-0f507d2623fe","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:54.968Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
